      "The first outside bug report in Picacho's life arrived — one user, one attached photo, three faults deep — and all three are fixed. First, with no character selected an attached reference was silently dropped and the render ignored it entirely (two independent faults, client and server, either fatal alone). Second, once the photo actually rode along, the image provider refused it: every reference was declared as 'reference.png' regardless of what it was, and her file was a JPEG inside an MPO container — the multi-picture format Android cameras and WhatsApp emit. Every reference is now normalized before it is sent: re-encoded to a plain JPEG (or PNG when it has transparency), rotation honoured, long edge capped at 2048px, and named for what it actually is. Third, those failed attempts charged a credit despite the promise that failed generations never use your credits — the rejection detector read only the LAST attempt, and this failure ended on the attempts-exhausted stub with the real rejections buried in attempts one and two. It now scans every attempt (and refuses the automatic refund if any attempt actually produced a billed render), covered by incident-replay tests, and the wrongly taken credit is restored.",
